<InteriorLayout title="Website Privacy | I.S Design + Build" description="How the current I.S Design + Build website handles project enquiry information." label="Privacy policy" headline="Your information. A clear explanation.">
  <Fragment slot="intro"><p>What this website does with the details you share.</p></Fragment>
  <section class="copy-section"><p class="cg-label">Website enquiries</p><div class="copy-body"><h2>The enquiry form</h2><p>When you send the enquiry form, the details you enter are emailed to I.S Design + Build through our website host and an email delivery service, so we can reply. The website does not keep a copy in a database.</p><p>If the form cannot send, it prepares the same text for you to send from your own email app instead. In that case nothing leaves your device until you send the email.</p><h2>Contacting the company</h2><p>If you email or call us, the information you share is used to respond to your question and discuss your project. Please share only information needed for that enquiry. A town or ZIP code is sufficient to begin discussing coverage.</p><h2>Website hosting and external links</h2><p>This site is hosted by Vercel, which processes technical request information to deliver and protect the website. Links to Google reviews and other external services take you to sites with their own privacy practices. Your email provider also processes messages sent through your email app.</p><h2>Website analytics</h2><p>This site uses Google Analytics to understand how visitors find and use it, such as which pages are viewed and the general location and type of device. Google processes this information and may use cookies or similar identifiers. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p><h2>Questions about your information</h2><p>Contact <a href="mailto:info@isdesignandbuild.com">info@isdesignandbuild.com</a> to ask about information you have shared or request its correction or deletion.</p></div></section>
</InteriorLayout>
